date:        2026-10-05 (same session)

The serial syscalls were made arch-neutral (a `serial_port` shim answers "no such
port" off x86) after the runs above, so the kernel was rebuilt and every lane was
re-run on the new image. Same markers, same results:

serial-x86 1/1, igb-x86 2/2, nic-x86 2/2, nvme-x86 3/3, x86_64-boot 9/9,
pcie-multibus-x86 2/2, ahci-x86 5/5, xhci-x86 4/4, iommu-dmar-x86 3/3,
driver-registration-contract 3/3, cellos-kernel 193/193.

The committed state was also compiled out-of-tree for every target this phase can
affect: x86_64, aarch64 board-rpi3, aarch64 board-rpi4, riscv64gc, cellos-boards,
hal-soc-x86 and the serial cell itself — zero errors.
